  2k_mercury.jpg  2k_venus_atmosphere.jpg  2k_earth_daymap.jpg  2k_earth_clouds.jpg  2k_moon.jpg
  2k_mars.jpg  2k_jupiter.jpg  2k_saturn.jpg  2k_uranus.jpg  2k_neptune.jpg

Changes made: none to the files. The game rescales each texture's brightness at render time so its
disc-integrated albedo equals the body's measured V-band geometric albedo (Mallama et al. 2017), and
composites Earth's cloud map over its day map; the brightness you see is the data's, the pattern and
colour are the texture's.

Source notes (Solar System Scope): the textures are based on NASA elevation and imagery data, with
colours tuned to true-colour spacecraft and Hubble images; unmapped regions are filled with fictional
terrain matching the surroundings, and colours are slightly more saturated than true colour.

